Build the immutable scope contract for this run before analyzing code. Extract exact in-scope assets/components, accepted impacts, exclusions, known issues, testing restrictions, payout priorities, and supplied deployment facts. Separate supplied evidence from missing facts. Never infer current program rules, live deployments, TVL, traffic, configuration, or severity from memory. A silent snapshot creates a scope gap.

Return exactly one record. Preserve the wording or a close identifier for each controlling rule so later agents can map a technical effect to a named accepted impact. Do not analyze vulnerabilities.

Create one report only for an eligible candidate with technical_verdict=supported and poc_verdict reproduced or deterministically_proven. Re-read every cited source location. Point file_path and line to the faulty operation or missing protection. Explain the attacker-controlled production path, the failed invariant, why every material guard fails, the observed impact, and the exact program mapping. Distinguish repository facts, supplied runtime facts, reproduction evidence, and remaining assumptions.

trigger_flow must be an ordered attacker-to-impact trace. malicious_input_example must be the smallest safe representation of the exploit condition for an authorized isolated target or local fork. Set exploitable=true only when the stated actor can complete the chain under the evidenced production configuration. Preserve root_bug_fingerprint, verdicts, asset, impact, severity, confidence, assumptions, and artifact references from the ranked record.

